# Criteria section 7: every declaration is checked as written, used or
# not. From bootstrap/examples/decl-nest-incomplete.moss:
#
# AssumesComplete for every kind (AUDIT-CHANGES #75): Box's nesting assumes
# f without f's requirement T (D20), as tests/errors/
# assume_missing_requirement_type.moss does for a fn's nesting.
# Verdicts: oracle accepts (check_assumes skips a tag's nesting); native
# accepts; Audit before accepts; now rejects (AssumedComplete: f's
# requirement T is not in force). Class B.
#
# The verdicts above predate the self-hosted compiler's check: it now
# rejects this too. The oracle still accepts it (a gap in agreement.rs).
type T;
assume T { fn f(); }
assume f { tag Box; }
fn main() {}
